meta {
  name: 03 Medicaid determination — two-member household
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v2/eligibility/medicaid/determination
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{api_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "metadata": {
      "caseId": "v2-medicaid-household"
    },
    "members": [
      {
        "id": "head",
        "dateOfBirth": "1990-03-15",
        "immigrantStatus": "citizen",
        "disabled": false,
        "pregnant": 0,
        "pregnancyEndDate": "2000-01-01",
        "receivesSsi": false,
        "isFullTimeStudent": false,
        "veteran": false,
        "hasDisabledChild": false,
        "monthlyHoursWorked": 80,
        "income": [
          {
            "type": "wages_and_salaries",
            "amount": 1200,
            "frequency": "monthly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "spouse",
        "dateOfBirth": "1992-07-20",
        "immigrantStatus": "citizen",
        "disabled": false,
        "pregnant": 0,
        "pregnancyEndDate": "2000-01-01",
        "receivesSsi": false,
        "isFullTimeStudent": false,
        "veteran": false,
        "hasDisabledChild": false,
        "monthlyHoursWorked": 80,
        "income": []
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Two-member household — one earner, one non-earner. Medicaid is
  member-scoped: the response has one determination per member. Field
  names come from the Medicaid rows of the engine-input catalog
  (immigrantStatus, disabled, ...) — the SNAP vocabulary
  (citizenshipImmigrationStatus, isHeadOfHousehold) is a different
  program's and would be rejected here. The spouse's explicit
  "income": [] answers the income question with "none"; omitting it
  would leave that determination pending.

  Expected: determinations[] with two entries, memberId "head" and
  "spouse", both status "approved" with medicaidCategory "adult" and
  chpEligible false (household MAGI of $1200/mo is under the adult
  limit for a household of two). Raise the income to see both members
  come back "ineligible"; drop the spouse's income key to see just that
  member go "pending" with its own missingInputs.
  Both members answer the category questions (pregnant, pregnancyEndDate,
  receivesSsi), work hours, and legal status: medicaid is no-guess end to
  end, and the pregnancy count feeds MAGI household size, so every
  member's FPL% waits on every member's pregnancy answer.
}
